      "body": "@l0rinc This makes sense to me. For the two cases (when a snapshot is activated and the current tip isn't in the snapshot's history), a possible fix would be to let the wallets know that the blocks up to the fork point were disconnected, thereby removing any stale confirmations immediately. In that case, the wallet could then ignore any disconnects from background validation, as it does currently with the blocks background validation connects to. This way neither of the two problems leaves the other one hanging. Curious whether this direction sounds reasonable, or whether there is a simpler solution I'm missing.",
