      "created_at": "2026-11-11T12:38:02Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-11T12:41:29Z",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "I reproduced the issue on master at commit `117c54d4c5` and tried the approach @ja7ad suggested.\nThe changes I tested (simplified) are below. The first prevents wallet notifications when disconnecting blocks during background validation. The second sends disconnect notifications for the blocks being replaced when the snapshot is activated.\n\n```diff\n// Chainstate::DisconnectTip\n- if (m_chainman.m_options.signals) {\n+ if (m_chainman.m_options.signals && !GetRole().historical) {\n\n// ChainstateManager::ActivateSnapshot (before AddChainstate)\n+ if (m_options.signals) {\n+     const CBlockIndex* fork{LastCommonAncestor(ActiveTip(), snapshot_start_block)};\n+     for (const CBlockIndex* pindex{ActiveTip()}; pindex != fork; pindex = pindex->pprev) {\n+         auto block{std::make_shared<CBlock>()};\n+         if (!m_blockman.ReadBlock(*block, *pindex)) break;\n+         m_options.signals->BlockDisconnected(block, pindex);\n+     }\n+ }\n```\n\nUsing the TODO values in the issue test as expectations, I got these results:\n\n- **Stale coinbase confirmations:** 200 on master, 0 with the change ✅\n- **`w` lastprocessedblock:** 199 on master, 399 with the change ✅\n- **`w` balance:** 0 on master, 34 with the change ✅\n- **`shared_tx` confirmations:** 0 on master, 0 with the change ❌\n\nThree of the four values now match the expected results. The remaining `shared_tx` failure doesn't seem to be caused by the stale block. I also tested without a stale block, and a wallet at height 199 when the snapshot is activated still doesn't process block 200 because it ignores historical `blockConnected` notifications.\nHow should we handle this gap? Should the wallet process the background blocks above its current tip, or should we trigger a rescan when background validation completes?\nI haven't opened a PR yet because I'd like to agree on the expected behaviour before proceeding.\n\nI know about the policy, I had trouble getting the Markdown columns to display correctly, so I sought help with the formatting @maflcko thanks",
